Why GRX rows can still be dropped

A claim row has to pass all of these before it reaches Pawan's WHERE. None of them were touched by the change.

l.source_system_sk IN (23,24) on the claim transaction.
Pawan took the policy-side SK values (23/24 for SF) and applied them to tclaim_transaction.source_system_sk.
The CIP claims proc filters on the policy's SK instead.
If your GRX claim transactions carry a different SK (e.g. 6/7 or something else), they fail.
I rank this as the most likely cause, because it's the one value assumed rather than verified.
JOIN tcustomer is an inner join in claims. Premium uses LEFT JOIN tcustomer. SF-sourced policies with a missing or non-matching customer_id load premium fine but lose all claims.
JOIN tclaim_features is an inner join. CIP claims use LEFT JOIN. A claim_feature_sk that is 0 or NULL, or has no row, drops the transaction.
LEFT JOIN tpolicy_type g combined with TRIM(g.policy_type_cd) <> 'HP'.
If tpolicy_type has no GRX row, g is NULL, the comparison evaluates to UNKNOWN, and the row is removed.
The LEFT JOIN acts like an inner join here.
LEFT JOIN tuw_company b combined with NOT IN ('51','61'). The same NULL behaviour applies if the GRX uw_co_cd has no match. It also drops the row if the GRX company's wins_uw_cd happens to end in 51 or 61.
Policy resolved through tclaim.policy_sk (d.policy_sk), not tclaim_transaction.policy_sk. CIP uses the transaction's own policy_sk. If tclaim.policy_sk is unset or points to a different policy row, a.source_system_nm fails.
Date and amount columns:
The date join uses tdate.month_acctng_ct. CIP uses pcs_month_acctng_ct. A transaction_dt_sk of 0 or -1 fails.
The amounts use loss_paid_am and expense_paid_am. CIP uses *_original_am. If SF writes only the original columns, <> 0 filters everything out.
One query to find the failing condition

Replace :ym with the month (e.g. 202609) and :claim_no with a GRX claim you know is missing from the feed. It returns one row per transaction and the first check it fails.

sql
SELECT t3.claim_sk, t3.source_system_sk AS tran_src_sk,
       t4.month_acctng_ct, t3.loss_paid_am, t3.loss_paid_original_am,
       t3.expense_paid_am, t3.loss_reserve_am, t3.expense_reserve_am,
       CASE
         WHEN t4.date_sk IS NULL                         THEN '1 transaction_dt_sk not in tdate'
         WHEN t4.month_acctng_ct IS NULL                 THEN '2 month_acctng_ct is NULL'
         WHEN d.claim_sk IS NULL                         THEN '3 no tclaim row'
         WHEN a.policy_sk IS NULL                        THEN '4 tclaim.policy_sk has no tpolicy row'
         WHEN tc.customer_id IS NULL                     THEN '5 tcustomer inner join fails'
         WHEN e.claim_feature_sk IS NULL                 THEN '6 tclaim_features inner join fails'
         WHEN g.policy_type_cd IS NULL                   THEN '7 no tpolicy_type row (<> HP is UNKNOWN)'
         WHEN b.uw_co_cd_1 IS NULL                       THEN '8 no tuw_company row (NOT IN is UNKNOWN)'
         WHEN TRIM(SUBSTR(b.wins_uw_cd,3,2)) IN ('51','61') THEN '9 company 51/61 excluded'
         WHEN t3.source_system_sk NOT IN (6,7,15,23,24)  THEN '10 tran source_system_sk not in list'
         WHEN t3.source_system_sk IN (23,24)
              AND TRIM(a.source_system_nm) NOT IN ('SF Admitted','SF Non-Admitted')
                                                         THEN '11 policy source_system_nm mismatch'
         WHEN t3.source_system_sk IN (23,24)
              AND TRIM(a.policy_type_cd) <> 'GRX'        THEN '12 policy_type_cd not GRX'
         WHEN t3.loss_paid_am = 0 AND t3.expense_paid_am = 0
              AND t3.loss_reserve_am = 0 AND t3.expense_reserve_am = 0
              AND t3.other_recovery_am = 0 AND t3.salvage_recovery_am = 0
              AND t3.subro_recovery_am = 0               THEN '13 all amount columns are 0'
         WHEN t4.month_acctng_ct > :ym                   THEN '14 future month'
         ELSE 'PASSES all filters (check month = ym for paid/recovery branches)'
       END AS first_failed_check
FROM   tclaim_transaction t3
LEFT JOIN tdate            t4 ON t3.transaction_dt_sk = t4.date_sk
LEFT JOIN tclaim           d  ON d.claim_sk = t3.claim_sk
LEFT JOIN tpolicy          a  ON a.policy_sk = d.policy_sk
LEFT JOIN tcustomer        tc ON tc.customer_id = a.customer_id
LEFT JOIN tclaim_features  e  ON t3.claim_feature_sk = e.claim_feature_sk
LEFT JOIN tpolicy_type     g  ON TRIM(a.policy_type_cd) = TRIM(g.policy_type_cd)
LEFT JOIN tuw_company      b  ON TRIM(a.uw_co_cd) = TRIM(b.uw_co_cd_1)
WHERE  t3.claim_sk IN (SELECT claim_sk FROM tclaim WHERE claim_no = :claim_no);

If this returns no rows, the claim isn't in tclaim at all, or claim_no has padding (try TRIM).

